1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LUNDMARK, ROLF V. - LUNDMARK, ROLF V. Rolf V. Lundmark, of Carmel, formerly of Hartsdale, NY, died May 21, 2005, he was 87. Rolf was born to Reinhold and Sigrid Lundmark on June 30, 1917 in Bergen, Norway. He is th
2 CONC e husband of the late Estelle Lundmark. He is the beloved stepfather of Robert Corey of Wichita, Kansas, Kathryn (George) Baum of Carmel, NY, Maureen (Kenneth) Gilleo of West Harrison, NY, eight grandchildren and 20 great-grandchi
2 CONC ldren. A brother Henning Lundmark died before him. Rolf was a proud member of the Norwegian American Ski Troops and served in the United States Army 99th Battalion, 474th Infantry. He worked at Sears in White Plains for over 40 ye
2 CONC ars and was a member of the Trinity Lutheran Church in White Plains. Rolf's favorite pastime was attending family functions and going out to dinner with friends and relatives. The importance of family was the central focus of his 
2 CONC life. Funeral Service will be held at Ferncliff Crematory Chapel Secor Road Hartsdale, Wednesday, May 25, at 10am. Friends may call from 5-9pm Tuesday at the Ballard-Durand Funeral Home 2 Maple Avenue at South Broadway, White Plai
2 CONC ns, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published: Monday, May 23rd, 2005
