1 OCCU Soldat
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johan Andersson adopted the name "Strid" (pronounced "Streed") when in the Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birger Sjöström in "A history of the family Mårtensson in Åsjön" writes that in 1845 Anders Andersson "sold the estate [in Åsjön]  to the former soldier Johan Strid." Johan Strid was a "Faltjagare". Lars Olof Sjöström writes:
2 CONT ""Fältjägare" is an older Swedish name for what you would call the infantry's Army rangers and the soldiers in these units. A field hunter is thus an infantry soldier in a unit specially trained for combat in wasteland terrain.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the year 1829 "Västerbottens regemente" was reorganized into "Västerbottens Fältjägarregemente" i.e. a regiment specially trained for combat in wasteland terrain. All soldiers in the regiment were therefore called fältjägare. 
2 CONC Johan Andersson Strid was accepted as a soldier in the Västerbotten regiment in 1826 and he was 20 years old and he was 5 feet and 9 inches tall, but he was exchanged in 1842. During his years as a soldier he lived in Bygdeträsk."
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan Anderson notes:
2 CONT ff mf; my great-great grandpa.
2 CONT The road to the village of Åsjön is "Stridsbäcken" (see photo). Photos of the road sign and his home site at Åsjön are attached as "memories" at his familysearch profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shown A1:1.366 (1794-1813) @ Blåliden, Nybygarre (settler),Degefors with parents +siblings Jonas, Greta, Johan Strid, Ana, Hans, & Ulrika; BUT family striken off, moving to Umeå.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupations: Soldier at Burtråsk ("Strid" means battle), jägaren (hunter) at Bygdeå; was a "Faltjagare."
2 CONT 1804-2? birthplace, Tjarntjarnliden, Burträsk, Västerbotten.
2 CONT 182? military service (soldier #89); both he and his wife are on p. 400; he from p. 394 and she from farm #1, p. 396 both moving to p.285.
2 CONT 1825-29 Farm #1 Ortoliden, Burträsk, A1:8B.400 (1828-35) w/parents +bride to p. 285.
2 CONT 1830 Risvattnet, Burträsk, A1:8B.396 w/spouse +3 daughters from p.285 to p.402; next door is  wife's parents, the Hedströms.
2 CONT 1831-1832 Mullberget, Burträsk; shown at A1:8B.402 w/ spouse +2 daughters to p.285.
2 CONT 1833-34 shown at A1:8A.285 @Åbyn w/ spouse+3 daughters, 1 son, from p.400 to  p.396.
2 CONT 1832 moved to Grundsunda, Västernorrland?
2 CONT 1835 in Brännbergsliden, p.553 Burträsk; son Johan Anton's birthplace.
2 CONT 1836-1840 at Åbyn, Burträsk, per A1:9A.318; daughter Anna Margareta's birthplace.
2 CONT 1840-11-24 move from Åbyn, Burträsk to Haggnäs, Bygdeå, per A1:9A.318.
2 CONT 1840-1845 Häggnäs, Bygdeå, A1:11A.116 (1838-45), from Burträsk, 1840-11-24, with wife, son, and 4 daughters; he is now listed not as soldier but "jägaren" (hunter).
2 CONT 1845-1894 at Åsjon, Bygdeå farm #1 where wife död, on p.81 in 1877; dotter moves in 1882 to remarry to Per M.
2 CONT Shown at Åsjon, A1:15C.683 (1874-84), as widower w/dotter +död husband #1; she is off to Grundunda in 1882.
2 CONT Shown on 1890 Swedish Census at Åsjön at his old Åsjön farm #1 as "undantagshjon" (a previous farm owner receiving support from the current farm owner). Strid is living with widower Johan Petter Sköld (b. 1835) family and Sköld's 
2 CONC 4 children (1890 census ID #4738115).
2 CONT Strid dies at age 89 in 1894 at Åsjön of "Alderdomsavtyning"  (infirmaties of old age).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT * Sveriges Dödbok 9 1815-2022, ID SDB7_06081486.
